    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f7be8c2_541967ec",
        "filename": "apex/apex.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 872,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-22T06:57:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this can be done there. When libA -\u003e libB and if libB is not available to the platform, we mark libA as such.  To do this, we need to traverse the tree in the bottom-up direction. Can we do that in GenerateAndroidBuildActions? WalkDeps doesn\u0027t seem to fit.",
      "parentUuid": "bee5bb5b_c33ba1b7",
      "revId": "991cebc3f35c809c3a9c08fdbff29c36967997f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74f9db3b_f16d3364",
        "filename": "apex/apex.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 872,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-22T20:26:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "GenerateAndroidBuildActions is always bottom-up, and you only need to visit your direct dependencies to propagate the value.",
      "parentUuid": "9f7be8c2_541967ec",
      "revId": "991cebc3f35c809c3a9c08fdbff29c36967997f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aae3f348_6973cad3",
        "filename": "apex/apex.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 872,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-23T01:26:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, but then I have to do this in all of GenerateAndroidBuildActions of module types that can be in APEX. That looks like a quite duplication.",
      "parentUuid": "74f9db3b_f16d3364",
      "revId": "991cebc3f35c809c3a9c08fdbff29c36967997f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d75a4ce_e2e3c759",
        "filename": "apex/apex.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 872,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-23T03:48:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You would have to call something on ApexModuleBase from each module that uses it.\n\nMaybe we need a mixin where module types can register functions to be called juist before GenerateAndroidBuildActions as a lightweight alternative to mutators.  Then InitApexModule can register it for all apex modules instead of having to visit every module and check if it implements the interface.",
      "parentUuid": "aae3f348_6973cad3",
      "revId": "991cebc3f35c809c3a9c08fdbff29c36967997f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec01c234_49b74950",
        "filename": "apex/apex.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 872,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-23T04:11:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having to manually call something on ApexModuleBase from each module is quite error-prone, isn\u0027t it? I don\u0027t understand why that is preferred over this mutator.\n\nThe mixin idea you suggested looks good; I expect it might be useful in some other places as well. But that seems to be out of scope of this change. Can I do that as a separate follow-up change?",
      "parentUuid": "8d75a4ce_e2e3c759",
      "revId": "991cebc3f35c809c3a9c08fdbff29c36967997f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
