      },
      "lineNbr": 884,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-24T00:31:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What should happen is that libstatssocket is part of the statsd module SDK and provided that way when these branches are built? (Specifically in the case of master-art it\u0027s probably more likely that there would be no dependency on libstatssocket at all when all the other SDKs are in place.) So the root problem is that proper SDKs aren\u0027t defined yet?\n\nIf so then I agree this is probably necessary for now. However, a ticket tracking it and a TODO here would be good. This exception seems a bit dicey to me.\n\nAlso, I misread the highlighted text - I read it as that the problem was when a lib only has apex_available:[\"com.android.something\"] and com.android.something isn\u0027t part of the build tree, so it got equivalent to apex_available:[], and that would somehow be a problem in itself. I suggest a bit of rephrasing to avoid that misconception.",
      "parentUuid": "527591d7_5d234729",
