      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-24T00:31:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So if we had an \"//apex_available:nowhere\" to signify that something can\u0027t go into either platform or any APEX we could use that instead of \"//apex_available:platform\" in these cases? Wouldn\u0027t that be somewhat useful to ensure that framework-all by some build bug doesn\u0027t end up in the system image after all?\n\n(Not saying it\u0027s something to address in this CL, just trying to understand the wider issue.)",
      "parentUuid": "d67fc14e_c32d0db8",
